  "grammar": [
    {
      "title": "Plural nouns",
      "titleVi": "Danh từ số nhiều",
      "en": "In Dutch the noun itself changes when there is more than one.\n• Words ending in -el, -er, -em, -en, -je get -s: appel → appels.\n• Words ending in a, o, u, i, y get -'s: euro → euro's.\n• Most other words get -en: tas → tassen, banaan → bananen.\nThe plural always uses de: de appels.",
      "vi": "Đa số danh từ thêm -en, nhưng: từ kết thúc bằng -el, -er, -em, -en, -je → thêm -s (appel → appels). Từ kết thúc bằng a, o, u, i, y → thêm -'s (euro → euro's). Còn lại đa số → -en (tas → tassen, banaan → bananen).\nSố nhiều luôn dùng de: de appels.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "nl": "één appel, twee appels",
          "en": "one apple, two apples"
        },
        {
          "nl": "één banaan, vijf bananen",
          "en": "one banana, five bananas"
        },
        {
          "nl": "één ei, zes eieren",
          "en": "one egg, six eggs"
        }
      ],
      "tip": "plural"
    },
    {
      "title": "geen = not a / no",
      "titleVi": "geen = không có",
      "en": "Use geen instead of niet before a noun with een or without an article: Ik heb een tas → Ik heb geen tas.",
      "vi": "Dùng geen thay cho niet trước danh từ có een hoặc không có mạo từ: Ik heb een tas → Ik heb geen tas (Tôi không có túi).",
      "examples": [
        {
          "nl": "Ik heb geen tas.",
          "en": "I don't have a bag."
        },
        {
          "nl": "Wij kopen geen melk.",
          "en": "We don't buy milk."
        }
      ],
      "tip": "negation"
    }
  ],
